# Off-machine pair for the hourly snapshots: the USB disk's hourly sd-db root
# to its own folder on the NAS, after every hourly snapshot (sd:4009).
# Copy to ~/.config/system/mirror-sync/mirrors-nas-hourly.conf ($SYSTEM_TOOLS_CONFIG/mirror-sync) and set your own paths.
# /Volumes/Offsite is a NAS share mounted over SMB, as in mirrors-nas.conf.
#
# Format matches mirrors.conf. Run this list ADDITIVE (MIRROR_SYNC_ADDITIVE=1):
# the local root keeps 24 snapshots, and the NAS folder keeps 7 days by checkpoint age.
# A promoted hub starts with one local snapshot, and an exact mirror would
# delete the NAS history it was restored from.
#
# The sd-db-backup-hourly job runs this list right after its snapshot, and only
# if the snapshot succeeded. offsite-verify restores the newest snapshot in
# sd-backups-hourly and fails when it is more than 3 hours old.
/Volumes/local/Backup Local/sd-backups|/Volumes/Offsite/Backup/sd-backups-hourly
